Theorem IA-T1: Per-field birth-site partition soundness

  Preconditions:
    - Phase-5 burden lowering keys per-(ArcVarId, FieldIdx) lineage nodes by
      birth-site: every node carries the birth-site (allocation) its field
      genuinely holds; distinct allocations carry distinct birth-site ids.
    - The same-allocation partition is a union-find built by folding an
      ADMITTED edge list. Two admission forms only: a Tier-1 unconditional
      same-allocation edge (fund / view / alias, whose meaning is
      birthSite(u) = birthSite(v)), and a phi-merge edge admitted ONLY under
      the singleton birth-site witness (exists B such that every phi
      predecessor argument x has birthSite(x) = B, and the merge node itself
      holds that B).
    - The union-find (functional parent map, fuelled find with the fuel
      carried on the structure, link-by-root union, edge-list fold) computes
      exactly the reflexive-symmetric-transitive closure of the admitted
      edges. This correspondence is DISCHARGED as a general kernel-checked
      theorem (not only on the Part D witness instances):
      buildPartitionUF_sameRep_iff_edgeConn proves both directions for every
      edge list, and buildPartitionUF_birthsite_sound composes it end-to-end
      with the closure soundness theorem. The fuel parameterization is the
      correctness-carrying design: fuel grows by one per union (link-by-root
      adds at most one non-trivial parent edge per union), so every parent
      chain stays within bound and the fuelled find always reaches its root.
      Consumers may rely on the executable partition as a proof surface.

  Soundness property:
    Forall node universe and forall birth-site map: SameRep(u, v) implies
    birthSite(u) = birthSite(v). Contrapositive: nodes with distinct
    birth-sites are NEVER placed in one representative class, so one balanced
    release per class cannot cross-free a different allocation. Kill-criterion:
    a phi merge whose predecessors carry distinct birth-sites has NO singleton
    witness, so no phi edge for it is admissible - a loop back-edge re-feeding
    a field from a different iteration's allocation cannot be falsely unified
    (the over-unification that would double-free is unrepresentable).

  Proof obligation:
    (P1) Per-edge admission soundness. Every admitted edge is birth-site-sound:
         a Tier-1 edge carries the equality by its meaning; a phi edge under
         the singleton witness carries birthSite(p) = B = birthSite(a) for the
         member predecessor a.
    (P2) Closure soundness (the partition-soundness theorem). By induction on
         the reflexive-symmetric-transitive closure of the admitted edges:
         refl is trivial, edge is (P1), symm and trans lift equality symmetry
         and transitivity. Parametric over the node universe and the
         birth-site map; through the kernel-checked executable-to-closure
         correspondence (buildPartitionUF_sameRep_iff_edgeConn, Preconditions)
         and its composition buildPartitionUF_birthsite_sound, the built
         partition only ever unions same-birth-site nodes.
    (P3) Kill-criterion. If two predecessors of one phi merge carry distinct
         birth-sites, no singleton witness B exists for that merge, so no phi
         edge is admissible: the over-unification is unrepresentable in the
         admission rule.
    (P4) Computed concrete witness. On the back-edge loop CFG (loop-invariant
         items field, loop-varying label field, aggregate move-alias class)
         the REAL executable union-find - the edge-list fold through
         link-by-root union and fuelled find, nothing hardcoded - computes:
         the singleton-admitted items header merge IS unified across the
         back-edge; the non-singleton label header merge keeps representatives
         distinct from both the entry and the latch allocations; the two
         distinct label allocations are never unified; the aggregate class
         holds no field allocation.
    (P5) Per-field release accounting over the loop. The cured per-field
         emission is safe across two iterations (no read-after-free flag, both
         field allocations net 0: items released once at exit, each
         per-iteration label released within its iteration); the whole-var
         single-dec emission leaks both fields (the negative witness).

    Machine-checked in the compiled Lean at
    aims-proof/lean/AimsProof/Partition.lean:
      partitionAdm_birthsite_sound        (P1)
      samerep_birthsite_sound             (P2 - the load-bearing theorem)
      distinct_birthsite_distinct_rep     (P2 contrapositive)
      buildPartitionUF_sameRep_iff_edgeConn (P2 - the general kernel-checked
        executable-to-closure correspondence, both directions)
      buildPartitionUF_birthsite_sound    (P2 - end-to-end composition:
        computed sameRep over any admitted edge list implies birth-site equality)
      distinct_birthsite_no_phi_admission (P3 - the kill-criterion guard)
      T1_items_header_unified_across_backedge, T1_backedge_keeps_distinct_from_entry,
        T1_backedge_keeps_distinct_from_latch, T1_distinct_label_allocs_not_unified,
        T1_agg_class_holds_no_field, T1_label_merge_no_singleton_witness (P4)
      T1_cured_loop_safe, T1_per_field_release_exactly_once_over_loop,
        T1_buggy_loop_leaks (P5)
      scc_external_source_determines      (P6 - the SCC flow witness: a
        strongly-connected phi-merge family whose every external predecessor
        is born at one site B holds only B-born values - strong induction
        over the entry depth to an external predecessor)
      scc_flow_witness_admits_phi         (P6 - corollary: with the family
        assigned B, each phi edge carries the standard singleton witness and
        admits under the EXISTING PartitionAdm.phi rule - no new admission
        rule; a witness-finding algorithm for the existing one)
      T1_per_field_birthsite_union_find_sound (conclusion bundle)
    The compiled Lean (verified by `lake build` under the trusted kernel) is the
    authoritative calculus; this .proof is the human-readable companion.

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (PRIMARY - induction on the RST closure of admitted edges)
      case_analysis (per-edge admission dichotomy: tier1 vs phi)
      fixpoint (union-find edge-list fold to its connected components)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: IA-category partition shape; the bespoke Rust checker's IA engines (structural_induction / fixpoint) are scaffold stubs (coverage-manifest.json IA expected_outcome = unimplemented_engine_shape). The authoritative machine-check is the compiled Lean AimsProof.Partition (lake build clean): samerep_birthsite_sound discharges the RST-closure partition soundness, distinct_birthsite_no_phi_admission is the kill-criterion guard, over the real edge-fold union-find witness.
